That's hardly a problem, though, since throwing daggers even at basic is
quite good enough. In fact, I'd probably use daggers anyway, unless you
make axes quite a bit better than them. After all, they're twice as
heavy. Also, they need to be more or less as common, starting from the
early game - and that includes being generated on Mine monsters. _And_
stackable, and not subject to being lost on hitting.

The obvious solution to the frequency problem is to take a hint from
Advent, and let dwarfs be generated with throwing axes instead of
daggers. That would be a perfect point for an Advent quotation, too
("The dwarf throws a little axe at you!"). Gnomes, hobbits and so on
would still be generated with daggers.
Ensuring that throwing axes won't be destroyed when they hit is trivial:
define them with a positive rather than a negative skill class[1].
Making them non-mergable is also a question of just setting a single
flag.

I do like this idea, though, but it does need a bit of polishing.

